From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:04:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 281/342] realtekwifi: RTL8822B false alarm counters and
 receive gain control

Linux's rtw88 reads and resets the PHY's counters and adjusts the receive gain
every 2 seconds. The port did neither: IGI stayed at 0x20 from the tables. With an
access point nearby, on signal 80 of 100, that is far too much gain. It's now
rtw_phy_stat_false_alarm() and rtw_phy_dig() from sc_set_rssi, as far as they
apply while associated.

On 2.4 GHz, in a busy band: 15 minutes of full load, about 10 MB/s each way, up
from 3-6 and 2-4, and no stall in 7.4 GB, where the chip had stopped receiving at
1 to 5 GB. 5 GHz still to be measured.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
